VERDICT: FIX-THEN-SHIP
FINDINGS:
🟠 [quorum-family-threshold] MUST-FIX Validator and engine derive the ">1 seat ⇒ families ≥ 2" threshold differently: the engine calls `terminalPanelCrossFamilySatisfied(panelRoster, reviewedSeats)` so the threshold keys off the REVIEWED subset, while `validateFinalPanelReceipt` uses `final_panel_seat_receipts.length > 1 || expectedMinimum > 1` (all dispatched rows). With `min_panel_size: 1` and two seats where one fails, the engine emits `final_panel_quorum_met: true` (1 reviewed seat, required=1) and the validator derives false (2 rows ⇒ required 2) → an engine-produced receipt is refused with `final_panel_quorum_flag_mismatch`, violating §1.1's "re-derive from the rows". Smallest fix: in the validator compute `panelRequiresDiversity` from `reviewedSeats.length > 1` (mirror the predicate's input), and add a receipt-suite case for min 1 / 2 seats / 1 failure.
🟠 [packet-hash-scope] MUST-FIX §1.1 and §2 require the validator's packet-hash all-or-none rule (`campaign-composition.js:416-433`, described in §0/§1 as running over every row) to be scoped to REVIEWED rows; the diff changes nothing in that block, and no §4.1 suite output is supplied. If the loop still iterates all rows, the standby receipt with a hash-less failed row (the new `failedNoHash` case) blocks on the packet-hash rule instead of passing. Smallest fix: iterate `reviewedSeats` in that block (or, if it already does, attach the green receipt-suite output as acceptance evidence for `receipt`).
🟠 [family-classifier-dup] MUST-FIX Intake seals `implementer_family` with a new copy `modelFamilyOfEngineName` (note the duplicated `(qwen|qoder)` line), while the panel recomputes the live digest with the engine's `modelFamilyOfEngine`; the drift comparison is only meaningful if both sides use one classifier. Any table difference makes every panel record `final_panel_roster_drift`/`roster_drift:true` with an unchanged roster, and seals `implementer_family:'unknown'` for that implementer, which disables the "one reviewed family ≠ implementer" gate. Smallest fix: export the engine's `modelFamilyOfEngine` (or move it to a shared module) and use it in intake; delete the copy; add an engine assertion that an undrifted roster yields no `roster_drift` on the `final_panel` row.
🟡 [reuse-branch-undefined] MUST-FIX In `runCampaignComposition` the `final_panel_gate_reused` branch copies `final_panel_quorum_met`, `sealed_required_review_families`, `implementer_family` unconditionally from `reusableJ.result`; a gate result persisted before this cut yields the keys with `undefined`, so the reused terminal object is neither legacy (key present) nor complete (not boolean) and `validateFinalPanelReceipt` returns `final_panel_metadata_incomplete` on a resume across the upgrade — contradicting §2's "receipts produced before this cut still validate". Smallest fix: spread the three fields with `hasOwnProperty` guards as the final receipt (`:2954`) already does.
🔵 [snapshot-before-claim] CUT/FOLLOW-UP The snapshot is written after the qualification block but before the `mission`/`campaign_contract` steps (step order now `qc_panel_snapshot,mission,…`), so an intake later rejected by claim/contract still seals the roster; the next attempt with a corrected roster records `live_drift` and reviews the stale seats. Spec §1.2 places the write here ("after the tier/probe/qualification block"), so not a defect against the spec; consider writing only on admission in 2-C.
🔵 [snapshot-digest-unverified] CUT/FOLLOW-UP On resume only `campaign_id`/`contract_digest` are checked; the snapshot's own `digest`, `seats` shape and `seats_complete` are not re-verified, and a snapshot with `seats_complete:false` makes the engine fall back to live seats while still skipping `finalPanelSeatQualified`. Spec requires only the identity check; harden later by verifying `digest` and refusing malformed snapshots.
🔵 [seats-complete-hardcoded] CUT/FOLLOW-UP `buildQcPanelSnapshot` hardcodes `seats_complete: true` regardless of `roster.qc_panel_seats_complete`; if intake ever snapshots an incomplete seat list the panel runs where base would have refused. Carry the roster flag (or snapshot only when it is true) — out of this cut if intake already gates `qcSeats` on completeness.
🔵 [step-order-message] CUT/FOLLOW-UP `implementation-campaign-state.test.sh` assertion text still says "contract validation occupies the second intake slot" after the expected order moved it to third; cosmetic.
